{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>No one shall eat of the holy thing.</b> Scripture speaks of terumah — the entire matter speaks of it." "<b>A priest's toshav and sakhir.</b> The toshav of a priest and his sakhir — therefore this 'toshav' is punctuated with a patach, because it is linked. And who is a toshav? This is a pierced-ear slave who is acquired by him until the Jubilee. And who is a sakhir? One acquired for a term of years that ends in the sixth year. Scripture comes and teaches you here that his body is not acquired by his master to eat of his terumah (Sifra; Yevamot 70)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:42.057576561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}